- op: discuss  # f6eb
  at: '2026-09-16T06:08:35Z'  # f6eb
  by: agent  # f6eb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f6eb
  clock: 3  # f6eb
  nonce: f6eb  # f6eb
  message: "Filed row FIXED, closing per the standing \"close on the filed row, file the\nresidual\" ruling. Verified by measurement on dev 81f1a69f88, not by reading.\n\nThis item's row is specifically io_primitives/*.yaml mapping to zero tests.\nAppending a line to io_primitives/rust.yaml and running `smart-test --manifest`\nnow selects 157 test files. The mechanism is the INV-muvis catalogue union at\nscripts/smart-test:1041-1052, and it took fix shape (b) from this item's own\nlist -- treat a data change as touching what loads it -- resolved by grepping\nthe test tree for load_catalog / io_primitives / io_boundary rather than by a\nhand-maintained map, which is what this item warned against.\n\nTHE RESIDUAL IS ALREADY CARRIED, so nothing new is filed: the catalogue union\ncovers 23 of the 169 shipped YAML files under packages/*/src, and the other 146\n(frameworks 107, dataflow_patterns 20, library_signatures 5, cfg_nodes 5,\nfunction_summaries 4, url_folding 2, taint_sources 2, taint_sanitizers 1) still\nselect zero -- measured. That belongs to INV-bigaz and INV-dohoj, whose\nstatements are about data files generally rather than this directory, and both\nhave been re-scoped with the enumeration today.\n\nThis item also asked \"check whether this folds INTO INV-kinin rather than\nstanding alone\". Answer, now that both are resolved: no. They were the same\nmechanism but took different fixes -- INV-kinin got a fixtures-path union at\nsmart-test:900-920, this got the catalogue union at :1041. Folding them would\nhave hidden that the second fix covers one directory."  # f6eb
